---
import Subpage from "../layouts/Subpage.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<Subpage
  title="Terms of use: free, open source, provided as is"
  description="The plain-language terms for unflub: free and open source under the MIT License, provided as is, anonymous usage stats on by default, automatic updates."
  crumb="Terms"
>
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="lead">Last updated <time datetime="2026-11-25">November 25, 2026</time>.</p>
  <p>
    These terms cover your use of unflub. They are short on purpose. By installing or using unflub, you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    unflub is made by Reimagine Media (<a href={SITE.org.url}>RMGN</a>), an unregistered studio in Ottawa, Canada, run by
    Matias Suxo. "We" and "us" on this page mean RMGN.
  </p>

  <h2>What unflub is</h2>
  <p>
    unflub is a Windows app that fixes typos as you type, in any app. Corrections are worked out on your computer. Nothing you
    type leaves it.
  </p>

  <h2>Free to use</h2>
  <p>unflub is free. There is no paid tier, no account and no ads.</p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>
    The code is published under the <a href={SITE.license}>MIT License</a>. You may use, copy, change and share it under that
    license. The unflub name and logo are <a href={SITE.trademarks}>trademarks of RMGN</a> and are not covered by it.
  </p>

  <h2>Provided as is</h2>
  <p>
    unflub is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. We work hard to make it fix the right words and leave the rest
    alone, but it can still get a word wrong.
  </p>
  <p>
    As far as the law allows, we are not liable for any loss or damage from using unflub. That includes text that was lost,
    changed or corrected wrongly. The MIT License says the same.
  </p>

  <h2>Check what you type</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for what you type and send. Read it over before it goes somewhere important, such as an email, a
    contract, a form or code. You can pause autocorrect, or leave an app out, at any time in Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Usage stats</h2>
  <p>
    unflub sends anonymous usage stats once a day. They are on by default and never include what you type. You can turn them
    off at any moment in Settings &gt; Privacy, and nothing more is sent after that. The
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> lists exactly what is sent.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    unflub checks for updates once a day and installs new versions automatically when you restart or quit it. Updates come
    only from our signed releases, and unflub checks the signature before it installs anything. You can turn off Automatic updates in Settings &gt; Privacy.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions, bugs and wrong fixes, <a href={SITE.issues}>open an issue on GitHub</a>. To report a security problem,
    please use <a href={SITE.securityReport}>a private report</a> instead, as our
    <a href={SITE.security}>security policy</a> describes.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there.</p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. When we do, the date at the top of this page changes. If you keep using unflub after a change,
    the new terms apply.
  </p>

  <p class="small note-legal">These are plain-language terms, not legal advice.</p>
</Subpage>

<style>
  .note-legal {
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
</style>
